8 0 obj
<<
/Author (United Nations: United Nations Commission on International Trade Law)
/CreationDate (D:20251205084415+01'00')
/Creator (Adobe InDesign 21.0 \(Macintosh\))
/Keywords (distributed ledger technology \(DLT\); blockchain; smart contracts; non-fungible tokens \(NFTs\); semi-fungible tokens; soulbound tokens; cryptocurrencies; decentralized autonomous organizations \(DAOs\); public permissionless ledger; private permissioned ledger; electronic transferable records)
/ModDate (D:20251205085934+01'00')
/Producer (Adobe PDF Library 18.0)
/Subject (This guide, prepared by the UNCITRAL secretariat, provides guidance on legal issues relating to the use of distributed ledger technology \(DLT\) in trade. It offers technical background, explains distinctive features such as persistence of information and interoperability, and addresses legal considerations for system selection, management, liability, and commercial deployment. The guide illustrates how UNCITRAL texts apply to DLT, includes use cases and case studies, and contains a glossary of technical terms. It is technology-neutral and aimed at commercial and non-commercial operators evaluating or implementing DLT-based services.)
/Title (Guide on legal issues relating to the use of distributed ledger technology in trade)
/Trapped /Unknown
>>
endobj
